examples:
  - ex-bonferroni-simultaneous-coverage-with-dependent-intervals
  - ex-discrete-superuniform-p-value-and-global-null
---

The examples identify the family and true-null indices explicitly. One finite model uses discrete superuniform p-values and a mixed configuration to compare FWER with FDR; another constructs confidence intervals with identical membership events to show that Bonferroni simultaneous coverage remains valid under dependence.
